Replace text using `s/pattern/replacement/`

<<<
```bash
sed 's/foo/bar/' file.txt

```

replaces the first "foo" with "bar" on each line.

[img[./files/images/linux/Screenshot from 2025-03-20 17-43-10.png]]
<<<

<<<Add g for global replacement:

```bash
sed 's/foo/bar/g' file.txt
```

[img[./files/images/linux/Screenshot from 2025-03-20 17-49-06.png]]

<<<


